    "Foreign institutions sold a net ₹944 crore and domestic institutions bought ₹1,924 crore (provisional). The rupee ended at a provisional 95.25 per dollar, and India's 10-year bond yield fell 5 basis points to 7.39%.",
    "Overseas, the Nasdaq fell 1.38% as Alphabet slid after its results, US GDP grew at a 3.4% annual rate, and the ECB and the Bank of Japan held rates. Brent settled at $114.88 a barrel."
