      "topic": "Global",
      "relevance": "On the radar",
      "headline": "The ECB held its deposit rate at 2.50% and said Christine Lagarde will step down in February",
      "what": "The European Central Bank left its key rates unchanged on 29 October, with the deposit facility rate at 2.50%. It said rising energy prices pose upside risks to inflation and downside risks to growth. Earlier that day it announced that President Christine Lagarde will step down on 7 February 2027, before her term ends.",
      "why": "Euro area rates move European bond yields and the euro, which feed into global portfolio flows and the rupee's rate against the euro. The euro area is also a large market for Indian exports.",
